      "problem": "The city of Baku, in Azerbaijan, is $91.8$ feet below sea level, while the city of Porto Alegre, in Brazil, is $16.4$ feet above sea level. What is the difference between the elevations of both cities?",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the difference between the elevations of both cities, we must calculate the difference between the city with the highest elevation and the city with the lowest elevation. That is, we must calculate $16.4-(-91.8).$ This gives\n\n$$\n16.4-(-91.8)=16.4+91.8=108.2\\,\\text{ft}.\n$$",
